[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "moemoekyun-bench-cycle1-260526", :doc/title "moemoekyun bench cycle 1 (2026-05-26 14:00 JST) — Phase 1 dataset registration + STEM baseline + evaluator fix", :doc/status "active", :doc/doc_type "reference", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# moemoekyun bench cycle 1 — 2026-05-26 14:00 JST\n\n**/loop fire** every 30 min (cron `13,43 * * * *`, job `c8acb432`).\n\nThis document captures the **first 30-minute cycle** progress per\nuser directive *\"bench ごとの dataset を datalad/ipfs でレポに保存 + baien-moemoekyun score を向上\"*.\n\n## Deliverables (cycle 1, ~30 min)\n\n### A. Phase 1 bench datasets registered to IPFS+DataLad substrate\n\n4 new datasets pinned via `e7m-dataset add` on mac-260317 (Kubo daemon\n127.0.0.1:5001, ETZ_DATASET_ROOT=/Volumes/260317/etzhayyim). All appended\nappend-only to `90-docs/baien/datasets.jsonl`; subdataset pointers advanced\nin DataLad superdataset `90-docs/baien/datasets/`:\n\n| Wave | Dataset | License | Size | IPFS map CID |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| W6 | `evalplus/humanevalplus` | Apache 2.0 | 14.4 MB | `bafkrei...` (Phase 3 coding bench) |\n| W7 | `edinburgh-dawg/mmlu-redux-2.0` | CC-BY 4.0 | 2.8 MB | `bafkreihayfi5dby...` (Phase 1 academic) |\n| W8 | `TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro` | MIT | 4.0 MB | `bafkreif36vlakb...` (Phase 1 academic, --max-bytes 80MB cap) |\n| W9 | `m-a-p/SuperGPQA` | CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 | 22.9 MB | `bafkreidl7baxpok...` (Phase 1 academic, Tier B/C) |\n\nTotal Phase 1 bench corpus: **44.1 MB** added to substrate.\n\n### B. Critical evaluator bug fix (single-letter MC scoring)\n\n**Root cause** (discovered cycle 1 via diagnose.py):\n\nThe earlier `loglikelihood(context, \"A\")` implementation returned **0.0 for\nall 4 options** when the continuation was a single letter, because\nBPE tokenization made `len(tokenize(context + \"A\")) == len(tokenize(context))`\nin many cases (the letter merged into the previous token). The function\nthen returned 0.0 (early return for cont_len ≤ 0), causing argmax to\nalways pick position 0 (letter A) — pure positional bias.\n\nThis produced the **uniform 28% accuracy across 5 different STEM subjects**\nobserved in the pre-fix sweep — exactly the \"always predict A → match when\nshuffled correct ≈ random 25%\" failure mode.\n\n**Fix** (`bench_gpqa_diamond.py` `loglikelihood()`):\n\nAdded `_next_token_logprob()` fallback that, when cont_len ≤ 0, directly\nscores the first continuation token (with leading space prefix for LLaMA-style\nBPE) via `log_softmax(logits[-1])[token_id]`. Now single-letter MC scoring\nreturns meaningful per-letter log-probs.\n\nDiagnostic (20 questions, college_physics):\n- Before fix: predictions = {0: 20} → 4/20 = 20% (random luck)\n- After fix:  predictions = {3: 14, 2: 2, 0: 3, 1: 1} → **9/20 = 45%**\n- **+25pp from evaluator fix alone**\n\n### C. Real STEM baseline (BitNet 2B 0-shot loglikelihood, fixed evaluator)\n\n5 MMLU-Redux 2.0 STEM subjects × 100q each = 500q total on Mac MPS, wall\n~12 min for full sweep. (vs earlier broken sweep showing \"<1s\" which was\nthe symptom of 0-returning loglikelihood — no actual forward passes scored.)\n\n| Subject | Broken eval (initial) | **Fixed eval (cycle 1)** | Δ from fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| college_physics | 28.0% | **41.0%** (+16pp vs random) | **+13pp** |\n| college_chemistry | 28.0% | **35.0%** (+10pp vs random) | +7pp |\n| college_biology | 28.0% | **54.0%** (+29pp vs random) | **+26pp** |\n| high_school_mathematics | 28.0% | **30.0%** (+5pp vs random) | +2pp |\n| college_mathematics | 28.0% | **29.0%** (+4pp vs random) | +1pp |\n| **STEM 5-subject average** | **28.0%** | **37.8%** | **+9.8pp** |\n\nWall time (real, post-fix): ~141 sec per 100q subject ≈ **1.4 sec/question** on\nMac MPS bf16 (4 forward passes/question × ~350ms each).\n\n### D. Honest interpretation\n\n- BitNet 2B's **actual capability** is higher than my broken evaluator suggested\n- **biology 54%** suggests model has decent science knowledge, mathematics ~30%\n  suggests math reasoning weakness (expected, frontier-non-goal per ADR-2605241900)\n- Reference 26-35B column (Qwen3.5/Gemma4) scores 80-90% on similar STEM →\n  ~2x gap; this matches the per-bench-plan expectation\n- The 5-subject average of **37.8% (0-shot)** is well above random 25% but well\n  below the Microsoft model card's reported 52% MMLU 5-shot —\n  **5-shot still expected to add ~15pp more** when EVO ROCm + lm-eval-harness\n  comes online\n- Math weakness (29-30% across 2 math subjects) → R2 corpus rebalance candidate:\n  boost `reasoning-distill-opus` from 10% → 20%, possibly add HMMT/AIME training\n  data when accessible\n\n## Score improvement attribution (cycle 1)\n\n| Source | Lift |\n|---|---|\n| Evaluator bug fix (single-letter loglik fallback) | **+9.8pp** average STEM baseline |\n| (Future cycles) 5-shot prompting via lm-eval-harness on EVO | ~+10-15pp expected |\n| (Future cycles) Chain-of-thought prompting | uncertain, +2-5pp expected |\n| (R1.4 train) coding-focused SFT | +3-10pp on coding benches; STEM unaffected |\n| (R2+ train) reasoning corpus expansion | +5pp on math/STEM expected |\n\n**Cycle 1 total**: **+9.8pp baseline lift** for free (measurement fix, no train).\n\n## Next cycle (will fire ~14:43 JST)\n\n1. Add 5-shot support to bench script (use cais/mmlu `dev` split for exemplars,\n   since MMLU-Redux 2.0 doesn't have dev split)\n2. Add Chain-of-Thought variant (`--cot` flag already exists, never validated)\n3. Run 5-shot baseline on same 5 STEM subjects, document lift\n4. Try one MMLU-Pro subject (broader coverage than MMLU-Redux per-subject)\n5. Try HumanEval+ (Phase 3 coding) — exec-graded, harder to scaffold but\n   may have quick smoke path\n", :doc/path "90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-bench-cycle1-260526.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "moemoekyun-bench-cycle1", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-26", :doc/date "2026-05-26", :doc/authoritative true, :doc/related ["moemoekyun-bench-plan-260526" "90-docs/baien/bench-snapshot-260526-bitnet2b-gpqa-diamond.jsonl" "70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/scripts/bench_gpqa_diamond.py"]}]
